Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["player absence", "offensive reorganization", "pre-absence initiation profile", "teammate usage redistribution", "primary play types", "initiator gain after absence"],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Can the closest-profile teammate be identified and shown to be the largest gainer in the absent player's primary play types?",
  "Are 11 absence cases (148 spells) enough for a test, given that spells within a case are not independent?",
  "Do play-type initiation measures have enough exposure and reliability to define profiles and gains?",
  "Does selecting the closest-profile teammate after observing the absence introduce regression to the mean?",
  "Are the play-type labels derived from play-by-play outcomes, so that the gain measure leaks outcome information?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-074",
   "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
   "finding": "Tested whether, after an elite creator's signature action, teammates score more on the next k possessions with the same lineup. All 8 creators at horizon 0. Jokic lag-1 ATT=+0.0282 CI[-0.043,+0.099] p=0.3779, recorded as a clean null on teammate PPP. Recorded as adequately powered (Jokic lag-1 n=1880; Giannis n=1804; Doncic n=325). A secondary Antetokounmpo result (+0.075 distinct initiators, perm p=0.0002, BH 0.003) is recorded only as a 'structure not eff' cut. Validation status recorded as no_validation_recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Connector absence versus usage-matched non-organizer absence on team offensive identity (D_A). Unmatched connector vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09, n=96 matched pairs. Recorded as limited by small sample and carrying MECHANICAL_FLOOR and SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER risks. Concerns identity disruption, not which teammate gains the absent player's initiations."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Catalogue of same-player and teammate X->Y sequential PPP premiums (for example P. George DRIVE->SPOT_UP +0.560, n=31, t=+2.2). Most cells recorded as DIRECT. Recorded as limited by label or classification error and small sample. It is a descriptive catalogue, not a test of absence-driven redistribution."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-032",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Teammate DRIVE preceding PNR. League-wide with calibrated PNR labels, +0.022 PPP, p=0.004 (n~180k). Inferrer-only ATT=-0.006, p=0.76. Recorded as artifact: the effect vanished once PNR labels were restricted to inferrer-only, attributed to calibrated-PNR temporal contamination. Recorded as limited by label or classification error, with a LABEL_ERROR risk."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-074",
   "what_failed": "Detecting a teammate-PPP lift from an elite creator's signature action, lineup-matched, at lags 1-3.",
   "why": "Recorded as an adequately powered null (B_powered_null): no elite creator produced a positive lineup-matched teammate-PPP lift at any lag. Shows that teammate-gain effects tied to creator actions were not detected in this data."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-032",
   "what_failed": "Detecting a PPP premium for teammate DRIVE-then-PNR sequences using play-type labels that included calibrated PNR labels.",
   "why": "Recorded as C_artifact: the apparent +0.022 effect came from calibrated-label temporal contamination and disappeared (-0.006, p=0.76) under inferrer-only labels. Play-type labelling is a documented failure point."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF40",
   "what_failed": "Ranking extreme same-player and teammate play-type sequence premiums as an effect catalogue.",
   "why": "Recorded as E_unclear (mechanism unclear), limited by label or classification error and small sample. Top and bottom cells were not stable enough to interpret as effects."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Play-type-based teammate PPP effects derived from this play-by-play are fragile. An apparent effect (FAM:SF-CHT-032) disappeared under stricter labelling, and an adequately powered lineup-matched test (FAM:SF-APPS-074) was null.",
  "Small-sample play-type sequence premiums were not interpretable (FAM:SF40), so per-player, per-sequence estimates from this data are noisy.",
  "A related absence-based question, connector absence on team identity, produced a supported result with a large usage-matched contrast (FAM:SF-APPS-088). Matching on usage was a workable design element for absence comparisons."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "None of the retrieved records tests whether the closest-profile teammate is the largest gainer in the absent player's primary play types. No retrieved record reports on this estimand.",
  "No retrieved record gives a validated estimate of profile-closeness, selection rules, or gain magnitude after absence of a specific player.",
  "The records do not show whether 11 absence cases with 148 spells can support a ranked teammate-gainer comparison.",
  "Validation status is not recorded for FAM:SF-APPS-074 or FAM:SF-CHT-032."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The effective sample is about 11 absence cases, not 148 spells. Spells within a case share the same absent player, teammates and lineup context, so spell-level tests overstate information.",
  "Choosing the teammate with the closest pre-absence profile, then checking whether that teammate gains most, combines a post-hoc selection with the outcome. Regression to the mean could make the highest-gain teammate look close simply because of noise in the profile.",
  "Three possible closeness criteria (profile, minutes, initiations, same-position minutes) create a researcher-degrees-of-freedom problem unless one is fixed in advance.",
  "Play-type primary types and gains are both computed from play-by-play initiator records, so the absent player's primary-type definition may be correlated with the outcome. Gains may partly reflect how types were assigned."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "Whether the 2025-26 partial season data (regular season before 2026-04-13, playoffs before 2026-06-21) are included, and how they are handled, is not stated.",
  "The number of absence events in each season, and whether the 11 cases are players or player-season episodes, is not stated.",
  "Exposure of each teammate to the absent player's primary types before and after absence is unknown.",
  "No retrieved record gives the reliability of play-type initiation measures at the per-player, per-season level.",
  "Retrieval returned four families, none matching the question directly. Further search_documents calls were not run."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "The retrieved records do not answer the question, but they show that play-type-derived teammate PPP effects have been artifacts (FAM:SF-CHT-032) or null under adequate power (FAM:SF-APPS-074), and that play-type catalogues on small samples are not interpretable (FAM:SF40). With 11 cases and a post-hoc closest-profile selection, the historical failure pattern supports not running the test as posed. The supported connector-absence result (FAM:SF-APPS-088) suggests a usage-matched absence design could be reused as a minimum viable test."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.2,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
    "text": "11 absence cases is too few for a ranked comparison among several teammates. Spells within a case are not independent."
   },
   {
    "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
    "text": "Choosing the closest-profile teammate after observing absence, then testing whether that teammate gains most, is subject to regression to the mean and selection on the outcome."
   },
   {
    "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
    "text": "Primary play types and gains are both derived from play-by-play initiator records, so the gain measure may be partly determined by the label definition."
   },
   {
    "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
    "text": "Per-teammate initiations in the absent player's primary types may be too sparse in 11 cases to rank teammates reliably."
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "no",
  "cited": ["FAM:SF-APPS-074", "FAM:SF-APPS-088", "FAM:SF40", "FAM:SF-CHT-032"],
  "summary": "No retrieved study tests whether the closest-profile teammate is the largest gainer in the absent player's primary types. The nearest records cover teammate PPP after creator actions (null, FAM:SF-APPS-074), connector absence and identity (supported, FAM:SF-APPS-088), play-type sequence premiums (descriptive, FAM:SF40), and a labelling artifact (FAM:SF-CHT-032). These inform design risks and one reusable design element, but do not answer the question."
 },
 "risks": [
  {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "11 absence cases; 148 spells are clustered within cases, so effective n is far below 148 and a ranked comparison among teammates will be underpowered."},
  {"code": "RTM_SELECTION", "text": "Closest-profile teammate chosen from noisy pre-absence measures and then judged on post-absence gain; regression to the mean will favour apparent gainers."},
  {"code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL", "text": "Primary types and post-absence gain both come from the same play-by-play initiator records; circularity inflates apparent gains."},
  {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "Derived play-type labels can be contaminated by calibration and temporal assignment, as in FAM:SF-CHT-032."},
  {"code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY", "text": "Per-teammate initiations in each primary type may be too few for reliable profile estimates, as seen in the small-n cells of FAM:SF40."},
  {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "Initiation profiles and minutes-based closeness may not be reliable across seasons; reliability has not been established."},
  {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Lineup, minutes, role changes and opponent strength during absence can change teammate initiations independently of closeness."},
  {"code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING", "text": "Several closeness criteria (profile, minutes, initiations, same-position minutes) and several play types create many comparisons."},
  {"code": "PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE", "text": "Without placebo absences or matched non-absence windows, the gain cannot be separated from ordinary teammate usage drift."},
  {"code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY", "text": "Seasons from 2022-23 to 2025-26 and partial 2025-26 data differ in roster and pace, so pooling risks drift artifacts."}
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.1,
  "rejected": 0.15,
  "untestable": 0.35,
  "artifact": 0.15,
  "uncertain": 0.25
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "As posed, the estimand is not well defined. Minimum viable estimand: among teammates ranked by a single pre-specified closeness criterion, the mean change in initiations for the absent player's primary play types, comparing absence spells with usage-matched non-absence windows.",
  "unit": "Team-player-spell (one absent player's spell, one teammate, one primary play type), with spells clustered by absence case.",
  "sample": "11 absence cases from the 2022-23 to 2025-26 regular season and playoffs data, using only complete seasons (2025-26 regular season after 2026-04-13; 2025-26 playoffs after 2026-06-21).",
  "power": "Not estimable with 11 cases; a power analysis must be run before any test. Expect the ranking test to be underpowered, so report effects with intervals rather than a pass/fail test.",
  "controls": "Pre-specify one closeness criterion (for example pre-absence initiation profile, computed over a fixed window separated from the absence). Match on usage, minutes, lineup and position. Use split-half reliability of initiation profiles. Use labels restricted to inferrer-only calls as in FAM:SF-CHT-032.",
  "falsification": "Placebo absences from matched non-absence windows; a random-teammate placebo; and a test that the closest-profile teammate does not gain more than the nearest-usage teammate under the same matching.",
  "multiplicity": "Single pre-registered closeness criterion and single primary play-type definition for the confirmatory test; other criteria reported as exploratory with a multiplicity correction.",
  "decision_rule": "Proceed to a confirmatory test only if split-half reliability of the profile measure and the placebo test both pass pre-registered thresholds. Otherwise report the question as untestable with this data.",
  "data_version": "Complete-season NBA 2022-23 to 2024-25 regular season and playoffs; 2025-26 regular season after 2026-04-13; 2025-26 playoffs after 2026-06-21. Partial-season files excluded."
 }
}

